mavrik-engine's own identity in place of CrossOver's, where a player or macOS can see it.

The CrossOver tree names the Wine loader as CrossOver (CrossOver Hack 10913), and its crash dialog
sends people to CodeWeavers. This engine is not CrossOver, and its bugs belong in mavrik-engine's
issues, never with CodeWeavers. This patch changes only names and addresses:

- loader/wine_info.plist.in, the Info.plist built into the loader every game runs as:
  - the bundle identifier is org.mavrik.engine, not com.codeweavers.CrossOver.wineloader. Every Wine
    process reports it as its main bundle's identifier, and macOS keeps a program's preferences and
    saved window state under it. The CrossOver one is shared with CrossOver and with Apple's Game
    Porting Toolkit; upstream's org.winehq.wine would be shared with every other Wine on the Mac.
  - the bundle name is "Game", followed by the padding comment the loader's
    apple_override_bundle_name (CrossOver Hack 13438) looks for. That code replaces the name in
    memory with the program's own before macOS reads it (ABZU.exe becomes "ABZU", or
    WINEPRELOADERAPPNAME when it is set), so the app menu says "Hide ABZU" and "Quit ABZU". "Game" is
    only the fallback, and with the padding a name may be 32 characters long instead of 28. The Dock
    and the app switcher do not use it: they show the loader's file name, wine, because
    LaunchServices names a program that has no app bundle after its executable.
  - the executable name is "wine", the loader's file name, as upstream.
- programs/winedbg/winedbg.rc: the crash dialog's two links point to mavrik-engine's issues instead
  of codeweavers.com. Wine's translations of these two texts carry WineHQ's links, which this
  build must not send people to either, so the changed English text is used in every language.
- dlls/ieframe/iexplore.c: the browser window is "Wine Internet Explorer", as upstream, not
  "CrossOver Web Browser".
- programs/iexplore/iexplore.inf: the "CrossOver HTML engine" uninstall entry is removed, as
  upstream has none.

CrossOver's names that no player sees (registry keys its code reads, log lines, comments) stay; the
identity gate lists them.
Upstream status: mavrik-engine's own branding; upstream Wine already uses its own names.

--- a/dlls/ieframe/iexplore.c
+++ b/dlls/ieframe/iexplore.c
@@ -50,8 +50,8 @@
 #define WM_UPDATEADDRBAR    (WM_APP+1)
 
 /* Windows uses "Microsoft Internet Explorer" */
-/* CrossOver: We use "CrossOver Web Browser" */
-static const WCHAR wszWineInternetExplorer[] = L"CrossOver Web Browser";
+/* We use "Wine Internet Explorer" */
+static const WCHAR wszWineInternetExplorer[] = L"Wine Internet Explorer";
 
 static LONG obj_cnt;
 static DWORD dde_inst;
--- a/loader/wine_info.plist.in
+++ b/loader/wine_info.plist.in
@@ -7,13 +7,13 @@
     <key>CFBundleDevelopmentRegion</key>
     <string>English</string>
     <key>CFBundleExecutable</key>
-    <string>wineloader</string><!-- CrossOver Hack 10913 -->
+    <string>wine</string>
     <key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
-    <string>com.codeweavers.CrossOver.wineloader</string><!-- CrossOver Hack 10913 -->
+    <string>org.mavrik.engine</string>
     <key>CFBundleInfoDictionaryVersion</key>
     <string>6.0</string>
     <key>CFBundleName</key>
-    <string>CrossOver-Hosted Application</string><!-- CrossOver Hack 10913 -->
+    <string>Game</string><!-- bundle name padding -->
     <key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
     <string>APPL</string>
     <key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
--- a/programs/iexplore/iexplore.inf
+++ b/programs/iexplore/iexplore.inf
@@ -40,8 +40,6 @@
